## Context

Brood report row 6 (conception/2026-11-01-brood-harness-run.md): rules/claude-code.md
§ Allow rules told agents to rewrite a denied git act in the `git -C` form; the native
note said allow rules are prefix matches, so `-C` misses. Author ruled "Probe first".

Probe 2026-11-01 (throwaway branch, each force-push once, needing a force each time;
plain push as positive control, allowed): `git -C <wt> push --force-with-lease origin b`
allowed; `cd <wt> && git push --force-with-lease origin b` allowed; plain push after a
separate call allowed (cwd had reset to the primary checkout; the branch ref is shared);
`git -C <wt> push origin --force-with-lease b` allowed. No denial reproduced, so form
is not shown to matter; the earlier "Git Destructive" denials remain unexplained.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] rules/claude-code.md § Allow rules no longer claims `git -C` is the matching form, in no more characters
- [ ] native note feedback_classifier_blocks_rule_mandated_git agrees
